+# fa_sliced_q - build, dispatch trace and validation commands
+
+This directory holds the supporting notes for the opt-in sliced-Q prototype.
+No command below has been run by the author of this lane; they are the exact
+commands the coordinator should run to compile, trace and validate.
+
+## Files
+
+- Shader: `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/flash_attn_cm1_slicedq.comp`
+- Generator hook: `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp:708-715`
+- Host gate: `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp` (search `TAG_FA_SLICEDQ`)
+- Existing test harness extension: `tests/test-backend-ops.cpp:10712-10723`
+
+## Opt-in flags (both default OFF)
+
+- `GGML_VK_FA_SLICEDQ=1` selects the prototype when its contract matches.
+- `GGML_VK_FA_KV_CONTIG=1` is required as well: the prototype consumes the
+  contiguous f16 K/V scratch layout produced by that existing path.
+
+When either flag is absent, dispatch is byte-identical to the previous path.
+If `GGML_VK_FA_SLICEDQ=1` is set but a shape disqualifies, the host replays the
+ordinary tuning, so the result is the same as with the flag off.
+
+## Standalone compile of the shader
+
+The generated pipeline is named `flash_attn_f32_f16_slicedq_cm1`. The exact
+glslc equivalent of the generator call is:
+
+```
+glslc -fshader-stage=compute --target-env=vulkan1.2 \
+  -D FLOAT_TYPE=float16_t -D FLOAT_TYPEV2=f16vec2 -D FLOAT_TYPEV4=f16vec4 \
+  -D FLOAT16=1 -D FLOAT_TYPE_MAX='float16_t(65504.0)' \
+  -D ACC_TYPE=float -D ACC_TYPEV2=vec2 -D ACC_TYPEV4=vec4 \
+  -D Q_TYPE=float -D D_TYPE=float -D D_TYPEV4=vec4 \
+  -D COOPMAT=1 -D SLICEDQ=1 -D DATA_A_IQ4_NL=1 \
+  -I ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders \
+  -o /tmp/flash_attn_f32_f16_slicedq_cm1.spv \
+  ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/flash_attn_cm1_slicedq.comp
+```
+
+The authoritative define list comes from `string_to_spv(...)` in
+`vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp` plus `fa_base_dict`.
+
+## Dispatch trace
+
+With `GGML_VK_FA_SLICEDQ=1 GGML_VK_FA_KV_CONTIG=1 GGML_VK_DEBUG_FA_TUNING=1`
+the host prints one `[FA_TUNING]` line per shape with `sliced_q=1`, and once
+`[FA_SLICEDQ] sliced-Q prototype active (D256, f16 KV, Br=64 Bc=64, rs=4, wg=256)`.
+If the line shows `sliced_q=0`, the shape fell back and the candidate was not
+dispatched.
+
+## Validation commands (not executed here)
+
+```
+# 1. Build with the Vulkan backend and the coopmat shader generation.
+cmake -B build -DGGML_VULKAN=ON -DGGML_VULKAN_COOPMAT_GLSLC_SUPPORT=ON
+cmake --build build -j
+
+# 2. Backend op tests, D256 tails, ordinary path (candidate disabled).
+./build/bin/test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT
+
+# 3. Same tests with the candidate enabled. Both env vars are required.
+GGML_VK_FA_SLICEDQ=1 GGML_VK_FA_KV_CONTIG=1 \
+  ./build/bin/test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT
+
+# 4. Trace that the candidate was actually selected (needs the debug knob).
+GGML_VK_FA_SLICEDQ=1 GGML_VK_FA_KV_CONTIG=1 GGML_VK_DEBUG_FA_TUNING=1 \
+  ./build/bin/test-backend-ops -o FLASH_ATTN_EXT 2>&1 | grep -E 'FA_SLICEDQ|sliced_q=1'
+```
+
+## What is NOT claimed
+
+- No SPIR-V was produced, no pipeline was created, no test was run here.
+- No register count, occupancy or speed result exists.
+- The direct `ColumnMajor` cooperative-matrix load of the K tile from a storage
+  buffer is not exercised elsewhere in the tree and must be validated at
+  pipeline creation; see REPORT.md blockers.
