--- /dev/null
+++ b/agent-notes/gdn_rms_scale/GDN-RMS-SCALE-NOTES.md
@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+# GDN RMS_NORM -> SCALE fusion - agent notes (gdn_rms_scale)
+
+STATUS: prototype (first patch), not production approved.
+
+## What this patch implements
+
+Opt-in Vulkan fusion `GGML_OP_RMS_NORM` -> `GGML_OP_SCALE`, enabled at backend
+init by `GGML_VK_FUSE_RMS_NORM_SCALE=1`. Default is unchanged (off).
+
+Files touched:
+
+- `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/rms_norm.comp`: new specialization
+  constant `do_scale` (id 2) and an epilogue that keeps the rms_norm rounding
+  into `D_TYPE`, then applies the SCALE formula `a * param1 + param2` with its
+  own rounding. `param2` carries the scale factor; the fuse only fires when the
+  bias is exactly `+0.0f`.
+- `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp`:
+  - new `pipeline_rms_norm_scale_f32` (same `rms_norm_f32` SPIR-V, spec
+    constants `{0, 0, 1}`);
+  - new `fuse_rms_norm_scale` context flag read from the env at backend init;
+  - new `ggml_vk_can_fuse` branch for `{RMS_NORM, SCALE}` with layout/alias
+    guards;
+  - new matcher branch `RMS_NORM_SCALE` with
+    `op_srcs_fused_elementwise[0]=[1]=true`;
+  - `ggml_vk_rms_norm` detects the fused SCALE, copies the scale factor into
+    `bin.param2`, and passes the new pipeline as an override.
+- `tests/test-backend-ops.cpp`: new `run_rms_norm_scale_exact` OFF/ON check,
+  called after the other exact slices.
+
+## Preserved semantics
+
+- The reduction tree is untouched. Only the epilogue changes. The rms_norm
+  result is still rounded into `D_TYPE` before the SCALE multiply.
+- The SCALE shader is `d = FLOAT_TYPE(a) * param1 + param2`. The fused branch
+  computes `D_TYPE(FLOAT_TYPE(tmp) * param2 + FLOAT_TYPE(0.0f))`, so the
+  rounding is the same as a separate SCALE with bias `+0.0f`.
+- A non-zero bias falls back. A `-0.0f` bias also falls back, because
+  `x * s + (-0.0f)` differs from `x * s + (+0.0f)` on signed zeros.
+
+## Guards (fall back to the unfused path)
+
+- rms_norm src0, rms_norm out and scale out must all be F32.
+- scale out must be contiguous; rms_norm src0 must have contiguous rows
+  (`nb[0] == type_size`). Real `nb[1]/nb[2]/nb[3]` strides are supported.
+- non-zero (or negative zero) bias.
+- `ctx->do_add_rms_partials` (the partials pipeline reuses `param3`; the fused
+  epilogue writes `param2`).
+- misaligned src0 or dst (`get_misalign_bytes != 0`).
+- partial overlap between a fused operand and the output is rejected by the
+  existing alias check; exact alias is safe (one workgroup per row reads the
+  whole row before writing).
+
+## NEXT STEP - 128-thread specialization (NOT implemented here)
+
+The current `rms_norm.comp` fixes `BLOCK_SIZE 512` and a shared-memory tree
+reduction with barriers, while the GDN Q/K L2 rows are only 128 wide. A
+specialization with 128 threads (one element per thread for width 128, no
+barrier tree, or a 4-lane subgroup reduction) could cut the reduction cost and
+the shared-memory traffic. This is a separate experiment:
+
+- It must be a distinct pipeline/spec constant; do not change the 512 path.
+- It must keep the same summation order (or prove and qualify the numerical
+  difference) before any model-level claim. Algebraic equivalence is not
+  enough.
+- Reuse the `run_rms_norm_scale_exact` OFF/ON harness plus a new OFF/ON pair
+  against the 512 reduction to qualify the change.
+
+## Validation (coordinator)
+
+Not compiled or run here. Suggested commands:
+
+```
+# build
+cmake --build build --target test-backend-ops
+
+# targeted OFF/ON composed slice (prints every case and a summary)
+GGML_VK_FUSE_RMS_NORM_SCALE=0 build/bin/test-backend-ops test -b Vulkan0 -o RMS_NORM_SCALE_EXACT
+GGML_VK_FUSE_RMS_NORM_SCALE=1 build/bin/test-backend-ops test -b Vulkan0 -o RMS_NORM_SCALE_EXACT
+
+# full Vulkan correctness run (defaults keep the fusion off)
+build/bin/test-backend-ops test -b Vulkan0
+
+# optional structural fusion proof
+GGML_VK_FUSE_DIAG=1 GGML_VK_FUSE_RMS_NORM_SCALE=1 build/bin/test-backend-ops test -b Vulkan0 -o RMS_NORM_SCALE_EXACT
+```
+
+Expected: the slice reports `RMS_NORM_SCALE_EXACT: N cases, 0 failed` and the
+fully fused cases produce bytes identical to the OFF run.
+
+## Open risks for the coordinator to check
+
+- Whether `minStorageBufferOffsetAlignment` on the target device divides the
+  256-byte view offset used by the slice (otherwise those cases fall back and
+  only the stride cases exercise the fusion).
+- Shader rebuild must pick up the new `do_scale` constant.
