@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+# MoE prefill: share count_experts - implementation notes
+
+This directory documents the opt-in patch for task `moe_counts`. It is not a
+test harness. The coordinator compiles and runs.
+
+## What the patch does
+
+`ggml_vk_mul_mat_id_q_f16` normally builds the hoisted routing table
+(`count_experts`) for every MUL_MAT_ID node. Gate and up read exactly the same
+`selected_experts` tensor. The patch adds one dedicated backend buffer,
+`prealloc_moe_count`, and a small per-execution signature. The first sibling
+dispatches `count_experts` into that buffer, the next sibling with the same
+signature skips the count and reads the same table.
+
+Controlled by `GGML_VK_MOE_COUNT_REUSE=1` (off by default, so both arms run in
+one binary).
+
+## Why a dedicated buffer and not `prealloc_split_k`
+
+`prealloc_split_k` is shared with dense split-K, FA scratch and GDN chunked
+scratch, and it is overwritten. A pointer/signature check on that scratch would
+depend on no intervening user, and the scheduler reorders independent nodes.
+The dedicated buffer is written by count producers only, so the table survives
+unrelated ops. Lifetime ends when another producer overwrites it or when the
+graph execution ends.
+
+## Invalidation
+
+Three independent guards:
+
+1. `ctx->moe_count_ids` is cleared at the top of `ggml_backend_vk_graph_compute`.
+   A replay that writes new IDs at the same address always recounts.
+2. The signature includes the IDs pointer, `nei0`, `nei1`, `nb[0]`, `nb[1]`,
+   the view offset and `n_as`. A different view, expert count or layout cannot
+   match.
+3. `ggml_vk_preallocate_buffers` clears the cache when it reallocates the
+   dedicated buffer.
+
+Before the producer writes it inserts a barrier when the previous table was
+read (`prealloc_moe_count_need_sync`), mirroring the existing `prealloc_*_need_sync`
+protocol. `ggml_vk_sync_buffers` resets that flag too.
+
+## Numerical identity
+
+The table only groups `(token, rank)` pairs by expert. The GEMM writes each row
+to the `(token, rank)` position it unpacks from the packed row id, so the
+within-expert order of `atomicAdd`s does not change any output element. Gate and
+up also keep their own weights, B tensor and epilogue, so reusing the table does
+not change the arithmetic of either projection. Activation-B conversion caching
+is untouched and its savings are not claimed here.
+
+## Scope
+
+- Hoisted tiled path only (`hoist_row_ids == true`). The vec/MMVQ path,
+  `ggml_vk_moe_gate_up_101`, and the non-hoisted path are unchanged.
+- gate/up, and also down when a call site presents the same IDs; the signature
+  is what admits a consumer, not the node name.
+
+## Rejected alternative
+
+Reusing `prealloc_split_k` and only skipping the count when the immediately
+previous node was a matching MUL_MAT_ID. It is smaller, but the split-K scratch
+is used by dense split-K, FA and GDN chunked, and `ggml_vk_graph_optimize`
+reorders independent nodes. A single intervening split-K would silently feed a
+stale table. The dedicated buffer removes that class of bug.
+
+## Validation commands (coordinator)
+
+Build the Vulkan backend and the eval test binary. Then:
+
+    # OFF arm (baseline behaviour)
+    ./build/bin/test-backend-ops test -b Vulkan0 -o MUL_MAT_ID_FUSION
+    ./build/bin/test-backend-ops test -b Vulkan0 -o MOE_GATE_UP_101
+
+    # ON arm (same binary; opt-in)
+    GGML_VK_MOE_COUNT_REUSE=1 ./build/bin/test-backend-ops test -b Vulkan0 -o MUL_MAT_ID_FUSION
+    GGML_VK_MOE_COUNT_REUSE=1 ./build/bin/test-backend-ops test -b Vulkan0 -o MOE_GATE_UP_101
+
+The new `test_moe_gate_up_101(512, ...)` cases are in the eval list. They push
+`nei1 = 512 > 8`, so they leave the vec path and reach
+`ggml_vk_mul_mat_id_q_f16`. Both ID strides 10 and 512 are covered. Compare the
+OFF and ON runs; the ON run must match the same NMSE tolerance.
+
+Model A/B (no quality claim from this directory):
+
+    GGML_VK_MOE_COUNT_REUSE=0 <serve>   # baseline
+    GGML_VK_MOE_COUNT_REUSE=1 <serve>   # candidate
+
+Keep weights, QSA budget, ten experts, strides and offsets unchanged. Measure
+prefill and small-delta with a no-trace run. The expected gain is two
+`count_experts` dispatches removed per admissible gate/up block; the time saving
+is not measured here.
+
+## Instrumentation if the count cost must be isolated
+
+If a profile must separate `count_experts` from the GEMM, add a diagnostic
+timestamp around the count dispatch in `ggml_vk_mul_mat_id_q_f16`, behind the
+existing profiler macros. Do not fold it into the production patch.
