@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@
+# MoE 101 deterministic replay protocol
+
+Support notes for the finishing pass. No build, GPU or test was run by the child agent.
+
+## What the harness proves
+
+`test_moe_gate_up_101` (tests/test-backend-ops.cpp) builds the production graph
+`MUL_MAT_ID(gate) + MUL_MAT_ID(up) + GLU(SWIGLU)` with the real 101 layout:
+A `[2560,640,512]` Q4_0_ROCMFP4_FAST, B `[2560,1|10,n]` F32, IDs I32 `[10,n,1,1]`
+with nb1 in {40, 2048} (stride 10 or 512), n in 1..8.
+
+IDs and B are a pure function of `seed` and `routing`, so the OFF and ON processes
+replay the same data. `GGML_VK_MOE_REPLAY_TRACE=1` prints a per-case `input_hash`;
+the hashes must match between the two arms.
+
+## Activation marker
+
+The Vulkan backend counts fused dispatches:
+
+```c
+ggml_backend_reg_get_proc_address(reg, "ggml_backend_vk_moe_gate_up_101_dispatch_count")
+```
+
+`test_case::eval` reads the counter before and after the whole-graph compute and
+requires:
+
+- `GGML_VK_MOE_GATE_UP_101=1`, admissible layout: exactly 1 dispatch.
+- `GGML_VK_MOE_GATE_UP_101=1`, guard / n=9 / invalid ID stride: exactly 0.
+- `GGML_VK_MOE_GATE_UP_101=0`: exactly 0 for every MoE case.
+
+This makes an unfused fallback fail the admissible cases, so a green run means the
+fused kernel actually ran. The check is serialized because the counter is process
+global and eval cases run in parallel.
+
+## Admissible vs fallback
+
+Admissible = `guard == 0 && 1 <= n <= 8 && ids_stride in {10, 512}`.
+Fallback = guard 1 (external consumer), guard 2 (intermediate view), guard 3 (LoRA),
+guard 4 (weight view), n=9, ids_stride 11 or 20.
+
+## Commands
+
+```bash
+GGML_VK_MOE_GATE_UP_101=0 GGML_VK_MOE_REPLAY_TRACE=1 build/bin/test-backend-ops -b Vulkan0 -o MOE_GATE_UP_101
+GGML_VK_MOE_GATE_UP_101=1 GGML_VK_MOE_REPLAY_TRACE=1 build/bin/test-backend-ops -b Vulkan0 -o MOE_GATE_UP_101
+```
+
+Expected: the same case count in both arms (34), all PASS, matching `input_hash`, and
+no `fusion dispatches = ...` failure line. The ON arm fails if an admissible case does
+not dispatch exactly once.
